# ── Bharat Maps — environment template ───────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in your real values.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables are inlined into the JS bundle at build time by
# babel-preset-expo (Expo SDK 57). After editing `.env`, restart Metro with
# cache cleared so the new value is picked up:
#   npx expo start -c
#
# ⚠️ SECURITY: because these are bundled into the shipped app, they are still
# extractable by anyone who unpacks the APK. Treat them as client-exposed and
# ALWAYS restrict the key in Google Cloud Console:
#   • API restrictions  → Places API (New) + Geocoding API only
#   • App restrictions  → Android apps → com.bharatmaps.app + your SHA-1
# For a truly secret key, route requests through your own backend proxy.

# Google Places API (New) key — powers Google search, place photos, ratings,
# phone/website and reverse geocoding. Leave blank to use the free fallbacks
# (Photon / OpenStreetMap Nominatim).
# Create one: https://console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PLACES_KEY=
